2.2.0
Home-agent WSL dry-run report (2026-08-29): the setup scripts now compute the "Remaining placeholders" report over the RENDERED content, so `--dry-run` prints the same list the real run does instead of exiting before it; `--build-cmd`/`--test-cmd`/`--format-cmd`/`--lint-cmd`/`--gate-cmd`/`--default-branch` work on every variant and an explicit flag always beats a variant-derived default (both scripts made explicit, not positional); `--wrap-existing-claude-md` keeps a consumer's existing CLAUDE.md by placing its full content inside the template's PROJECT-CUSTOM region instead of skipping the file, and a plain skip now names the flag; `templates/*/gitignore` moved the inline comment off the `/.mcp.json` line (an inline `#` is part of a gitignore pattern, so the rule never matched); the `{{DB_FILENAME}}`/`{{DB_DIRECTORY}}` SQLite paragraph is gone from the five variants that never ask for DB values; CLAUDE.local.md states each MCP server applies only if registered and GitHub ops fall back to the `gh` CLI; PROJECT_CONTEXT.md carries `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` plus an optional `**Protected branches**:` line; the autoMode snippet is neutrally worded. Fix round 1: setup-project.ps1 copies `hooks/` RECURSIVELY (the non-recursive `*.sh` copy never copied `hooks/lib/git-cmd.sh`, so every gate failed closed on a Windows-bootstrapped project), the `.gitignore` merge matches whole lines instead of substrings (`.claude/.mcp.json` contains `/.mcp.json`, so the root rule was never appended on an upgrade), `--default-branch` detection requires the target to BE the repo root and prefers `origin/HEAD` over the checked-out branch, and `--force` + `--wrap-existing-claude-md` is now a hard error. 12 hook scripts + `hooks/lib/`, 8 skills.
